#IncidentPostmortem

Day 22: Service Routing Failed After Deployment

Incident:
Deployment completed, but users saw old behavior for 15 minutes.


What Happened Next:
Service endpoints did not update to include new pods.


Root Cause:
1. Label Mismatch: Pods had app=v2, Service selector expected app=v1.
2. Service Uses Labels Only: Kubernetes Services ignore deployments and versions.


Fix:
 1. Aligned pod labels with Service selector.
 2. Verified endpoint updates post-deploy.


Takeaway:
In Kubernetes, labels decide traffic flow.
